WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.768 --> 00:00:04.204
Nearly $1 million in sanctions.

00:00:04.237 --> 00:00:05.071
That's what a federal judge

00:00:05.071 --> 00:00:05.939
is ordering former

00:00:05.939 --> 00:00:06.706
President Trump

00:00:06.706 --> 00:00:07.941
and one of his lawyers

00:00:07.941 --> 00:00:09.709
to pay it over a lawsuit

00:00:09.709 --> 00:00:11.945
they filed against Hillary Clinton,

00:00:11.945 --> 00:00:13.213
former top Justice Party

00:00:13.213 --> 00:00:14.848
officials and several others

00:00:14.848 --> 00:00:16.883
alleging that the nearly three dozen

00:00:16.883 --> 00:00:17.484
defendants

00:00:17.484 --> 00:00:19.052
conspired against Trump

00:00:19.052 --> 00:00:21.087
in the 2016 campaign.

00:00:21.087 --> 00:00:21.821
Judge Donald

00:00:21.821 --> 00:00:22.789
Middlebrook issuing

00:00:22.789 --> 00:00:25.058
a scathing rebuke of the case,

00:00:25.058 --> 00:00:26.126
writing, quote,

00:00:26.126 --> 00:00:28.194
This case should never have been brought.

00:00:28.495 --> 00:00:29.863
Its inadequacy

00:00:29.863 --> 00:00:31.097
as a legal claim

00:00:31.097 --> 00:00:33.099
was evident from the start.

00:00:33.099 --> 00:00:35.902
No reasonable lawyer would have filed it,

00:00:36.269 --> 00:00:37.470
ripping some of Trump's

00:00:37.470 --> 00:00:40.507
claims, writing, quote, It was not that

00:00:40.507 --> 00:00:41.941
the complaint and amended

00:00:41.941 --> 00:00:44.210
complaint were inadequate in any respect.

00:00:44.477 --> 00:00:46.012
They were inadequate in nearly

00:00:46.012 --> 00:00:47.647
every respect.

00:00:47.647 --> 00:00:49.049
And pointing out Trump's habit

00:00:49.049 --> 00:00:51.317
of using the courts for his own purposes.

00:00:51.584 --> 00:00:52.619
Writing Mr.

00:00:52.619 --> 00:00:54.120
Trump is a prolific

00:00:54.120 --> 00:00:55.989
and sophisticated litigant

00:00:55.989 --> 00:00:57.991
who was repeatedly using the courts

00:00:58.291 --> 00:01:00.994
to seek revenge on political adversaries.

00:01:01.227 --> 00:01:02.896
He is the mastermind

00:01:02.896 --> 00:01:04.497
of strategic abuse

00:01:04.497 --> 00:01:05.932
of the judicial process,

00:01:05.932 --> 00:01:08.001
and he cannot be seen as a litigant

00:01:08.201 --> 00:01:10.770
blindly following the advice of a lawyer.

00:01:11.004 --> 00:01:11.838
He knew full

00:01:11.838 --> 00:01:14.340
well the impact of his actions.

00:01:14.674 --> 00:01:16.976
And as of tonight, Trump and his team

00:01:16.976 --> 00:01:18.778
have dropped another lawsuit.

00:01:18.778 --> 00:01:21.047
They filed that one against New York

00:01:21.047 --> 00:01:22.882
Attorney General Letitia James.

00:01:22.882 --> 00:01:23.783
For more on all of this,

00:01:23.783 --> 00:01:25.185
I want to bring in CNN legal analyst

00:01:25.185 --> 00:01:26.152
Elliott Williams

00:01:26.152 --> 00:01:26.920
and Donald Trump

00:01:26.920 --> 00:01:29.055
biographer Michael D'Antonio.

00:01:29.222 --> 00:01:30.490
Glad to see you both here.

00:01:30.490 --> 00:01:31.724
First of all, Eliot,

00:01:31.724 --> 00:01:32.892
this judge was not mincing

00:01:32.892 --> 00:01:37.063
any words in his review of this lawsuit.

00:01:37.097 --> 00:01:38.531
What was your reaction?

00:01:38.531 --> 00:01:39.199
Well, first off,

00:01:39.199 --> 00:01:39.766
you know, I clerked

00:01:39.766 --> 00:01:41.434
for Judge Middlebrooks.

00:01:41.434 --> 00:01:44.070
In a past life, maybe 20 years ago.

00:01:44.070 --> 00:01:45.071
And so, you know,

00:01:45.071 --> 00:01:47.373
I've seen his opinions over the years.

00:01:47.507 --> 00:01:49.008
This was a very remarkable opinion.

00:01:49.008 --> 00:01:49.742
And I think

00:01:49.742 --> 00:01:50.810
there's a lot of focus

00:01:50.810 --> 00:01:53.079
on sort of the bombast and the,

00:01:53.613 --> 00:01:55.682
you know, Trump versus the law.

00:01:55.682 --> 00:01:57.050
This is actually a very meticulous

00:01:57.050 --> 00:01:58.351
legal opinion

00:01:58.351 --> 00:02:00.220
laying out the standard

00:02:00.220 --> 00:02:01.821
for when you sanction an attorney,

00:02:01.821 --> 00:02:02.655
what it takes,

00:02:02.655 --> 00:02:04.257
how they calculate the fees

00:02:04.257 --> 00:02:06.392
and what the law says and what.

00:02:06.392 --> 00:02:08.561
And also, looking back at past conduct,

00:02:09.095 --> 00:02:09.362
you know,

00:02:09.362 --> 00:02:10.196
they point out the fact

00:02:10.196 --> 00:02:11.598
that the former president sued

00:02:11.598 --> 00:02:13.399
the Pulitzer board

00:02:13.399 --> 00:02:15.835
over the fact that the Pulitzers

00:02:15.835 --> 00:02:16.169
were given

00:02:16.169 --> 00:02:16.903
to The New York Times,

00:02:16.903 --> 00:02:17.971
The Washington Post,

00:02:17.971 --> 00:02:18.938
in making a case

00:02:18.938 --> 00:02:21.107
that this was just a frivolous lawsuit.

00:02:21.141 --> 00:02:23.209
And now we should also note this.

00:02:23.209 --> 00:02:25.211
900 plus thousand dollars.

00:02:25.211 --> 00:02:26.179
It wasn't just a number

00:02:26.179 --> 00:02:27.213
pulled out of thin air.

00:02:27.213 --> 00:02:29.215
It's for attorney's fees. And costs.

00:02:29.215 --> 00:02:30.416
And the judge walks through

00:02:30.416 --> 00:02:32.285
and again, in great detail

00:02:32.285 --> 00:02:34.387
how you tabulate that $1 million.

00:02:34.387 --> 00:02:35.021
So it's not

00:02:35.021 --> 00:02:36.723
I think folks have in their head

00:02:36.723 --> 00:02:37.957
that this judge just got mad

00:02:37.957 --> 00:02:38.958
at Donald Trump

00:02:38.958 --> 00:02:41.427
and then threw $1,000,000 fine at him.

00:02:41.528 --> 00:02:42.996
It's just it's far more complicated

00:02:42.996 --> 00:02:44.731
and legally supported than that.

00:02:44.731 --> 00:02:45.165
Michael,

00:02:45.165 --> 00:02:47.167
it almost seems he's talking about this

00:02:47.167 --> 00:02:48.334
and you hear about it in the press

00:02:48.334 --> 00:02:48.835
the idea

00:02:48.835 --> 00:02:51.070
and you've written about the idea of

00:02:51.070 --> 00:02:51.738
sort of the Trump

00:02:51.738 --> 00:02:52.972
playbook, so to speak,

00:02:52.972 --> 00:02:55.074
the idea of some litigants

00:02:55.074 --> 00:02:56.342
essentially not being able

00:02:56.342 --> 00:02:58.111
to go against the best lawyers

00:02:58.111 --> 00:02:59.879
that money can possibly buy.

00:02:59.879 --> 00:03:01.247
What is your reaction to this?

00:03:02.582 --> 00:03:03.449
Well, I do

00:03:03.449 --> 00:03:06.452
think that the judge has noted

00:03:06.853 --> 00:03:09.589
one of the constant themes

00:03:09.589 --> 00:03:10.657
when you examine

00:03:10.657 --> 00:03:13.193
Donald Trump's tactics and methods,

00:03:13.760 --> 00:03:16.596
he sues people for a variety of reasons

00:03:16.596 --> 00:03:17.297
and rarely

00:03:17.297 --> 00:03:18.331
does that have anything

00:03:18.331 --> 00:03:20.133
to do with justice.

00:03:20.133 --> 00:03:21.868
He wants to punish people

00:03:21.868 --> 00:03:23.903
by draining their bank accounts.

00:03:23.903 --> 00:03:26.406
He wants to attract publicity

00:03:26.673 --> 00:03:28.308
and he wants to deflect

00:03:28.308 --> 00:03:30.043
the public's attention

00:03:30.043 --> 00:03:32.579
from his own misdeeds.

00:03:32.579 --> 00:03:35.882
So the very first lawsuit he ever filed

00:03:35.882 --> 00:03:40.286
was in 1973 when he had his pit bull.

00:03:40.286 --> 00:03:43.289
Roy Cohn alleged that the Justice

00:03:43.289 --> 00:03:46.292
Department had acted as a Gestapo force

00:03:46.593 --> 00:03:47.760
in trying to get him

00:03:47.760 --> 00:03:48.361
to stop

00:03:48.361 --> 00:03:49.762
discriminating against

00:03:49.762 --> 00:03:51.864
minority applicants for apartments.

00:03:52.432 --> 00:03:55.935
I think the judge noted many cases

00:03:55.935 --> 00:03:59.005
where Trump has done similar things.

00:03:59.038 --> 00:04:00.940
I think he could write his own

00:04:00.940 --> 00:04:02.942
biography of Donald Trump,

00:04:02.942 --> 00:04:05.712
given what I've seen in the ruling.

00:04:06.045 --> 00:04:08.281
So he got it all right.

00:04:08.781 --> 00:04:11.217
He was one of the rare

00:04:11.217 --> 00:04:14.821
places where Trump met accountability.

00:04:14.821 --> 00:04:15.989
And this is something

00:04:15.989 --> 00:04:17.991
people ask about all the time.

00:04:18.291 --> 00:04:20.526
When will this man be held accountable?

00:04:20.560 --> 00:04:21.527
Well, here

00:04:21.527 --> 00:04:23.596
is one case where he has been

00:04:23.596 --> 00:04:25.265
held accountable.

00:04:25.265 --> 00:04:25.865
Elliot

00:04:25.865 --> 00:04:28.201
is this telling about his approach

00:04:28.201 --> 00:04:30.069
that we've talked about more broadly

00:04:30.069 --> 00:04:31.971
and how he views lawyers

00:04:31.971 --> 00:04:33.206
or even the justice system

00:04:33.206 --> 00:04:33.806
when he was the head

00:04:33.806 --> 00:04:34.741
of the executive branch?

00:04:34.741 --> 00:04:35.742
Yeah, you know, it's interesting

00:04:35.742 --> 00:04:35.942
you know,

00:04:35.942 --> 00:04:37.343
and we talk about this idea of

00:04:37.343 --> 00:04:38.478
when will this person

00:04:38.478 --> 00:04:39.345
be held accountable.

00:04:39.345 --> 00:04:40.913
You ought to sort of treat

00:04:40.913 --> 00:04:42.615
every instance as unique.

00:04:42.615 --> 00:04:42.815
You know,

00:04:42.815 --> 00:04:43.783
the fact that

00:04:43.783 --> 00:04:44.450
one person

00:04:44.450 --> 00:04:45.285
is suing Donald Trump

00:04:45.285 --> 00:04:46.252
for one jurisdiction

00:04:46.252 --> 00:04:47.887
is seeking to prosecute them.

00:04:47.887 --> 00:04:49.522
They all get sort of mixed together.

00:04:49.522 --> 00:04:50.523
And, you know,

00:04:50.523 --> 00:04:51.624
I think an opinion like this

00:04:51.624 --> 00:04:52.659
is very important

00:04:52.659 --> 00:04:53.860
and sort of,

00:04:53.860 --> 00:04:56.462
you know, in isolation in this case,

00:04:56.462 --> 00:04:58.531
what we've seen is how

00:04:58.531 --> 00:05:00.533
you can sort of lay out a case,

00:05:01.501 --> 00:05:01.768
you know,

00:05:01.768 --> 00:05:04.370
based on the facts and law in one matter

00:05:04.370 --> 00:05:06.272
as opposed to pulling everything else.

00:05:06.272 --> 00:05:08.408
And so, you know, it was just

00:05:08.408 --> 00:05:09.842
I think it was very powerfully written

00:05:09.842 --> 00:05:12.312
and well-reasoned and organized.

00:05:12.312 --> 00:05:13.680
And I think that just should be noted.

00:05:13.680 --> 00:05:15.648
And it's true of the idea of conflation

00:05:15.648 --> 00:05:17.784
being a dangerous vehicle, especially.

00:05:17.784 --> 00:05:18.751
We'll talk about Donald Trump.

00:05:18.751 --> 00:05:20.019
Everything seems to come together

00:05:20.019 --> 00:05:21.688
and they go, it is part of this.

00:05:21.688 --> 00:05:23.589
And this judge seemed to make very clear

00:05:23.589 --> 00:05:25.458
is about this case in this moment.

00:05:25.458 --> 00:05:26.659
Thank you so much, everyone.

